<p>When a document is scanned for printing, its size might be detected 
 as larger than the original, and a printer error might occur.</p>
<p>This function prevents this problem.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>If a custom paper size is selected in the <span class="Term-Soft">Document Size:</span> list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Basic</span> 
 menu, it is automatically changed to A4.</p></li>
<li><p>If a custom paper size is selected in <span class="Term-Soft">Print 
 On:</span>, it is automatically changed to <span class="Term-Soft">Same 
 as Original Size</span>.</p></li>
</ul>
<ol>
<li><p>Open the printing preferences dialog box after 
 opening a scanned document from an application.</p></li>
<li><p>Click the <span class="Term-Soft">Driver Options</span> 
 menu on the <span class="Term-Soft">Detailed Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>Select the <span class="Term-Soft">Near Standard 
 Size</span> check box.</p></li>
<li><p>Select a standard size in the <span class="Term-Soft">Document 
 Size:</span> list on the <span class="Term-Soft">Basic</span> menu.<br/>
 You can also select from the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used 
 Settings</span> tab.</p></li>
<li><p>After making any other necessary settings, click 
 <span class="Term-OS">OK</span> to close the printing preferences dialog 
 box.</p></li>
<li><p>Start printing.</p></li>
</ol>
